This fixture is DISTRIBUTION-ONLY. It must never be copied to a consumer.

It is shard 'c' of review-shard-merge-mutants, and it inherits that fixture's reason without
restating it: it is the MUTATION BATTERY behind the shipped review-shard-merge fixture, editing
copies of core's own partition-review-diff.sh and merge-review-shards.sh in temp trees, so every
verdict is a question about whether THIS repository's arms still discriminate.

A shard is a scheduling boundary, never a subject boundary, so it can carry no ship decision
its sibling does not. On a consumer it would be a unit the consumer cannot act on, sitting in
that consumer's suite schedule.
